            <chunk name="Object" index="30">
              <items count="2">
                <item name="GUID" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">59e0b89a-e487-49f8-bab8-b5bab16be14c</item>
                <item name="Name" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Panel</item>
              </items>
              <chunks count="1">
                <chunk name="Container">
                  <items count="8">
                    <item name="Description" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">A panel for custom notes and text values</item>
                    <item name="InstanceGuid" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">6de71dc4-a3f4-5c4f-aa91-8b1fac5ced7d</item>
                    <item name="Name" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Panel</item>
                    <item name="NickName" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">README</item>
                    <item name="Optional" type_name="gh_bool" type_code="1">false</item>
                    <item name="ScrollRatio" type_name="gh_double" type_code="6">0</item>
                    <item name="SourceCount" type_name="gh_int32" type_code="3">0</item>
                    <item name="UserText" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">LOUVRES ROTATED BY LENGTH

A row of blades of increasing length is rotated so each blade's angle follows its own length: short blades stay flat, long blades turn - the logic behind graded shading louvres.

HOW TO USE
1. 'Blade count' sets the number of blades; 'Base length', 'Growth step' and 'Growth power' shape how blade lengths grow along the row.
2. Edit the two small panels to set the angle range in multiples of pi - 0.5 means a quarter turn.
3. Bake 'Rotate' to get the rotated blades (the unrotated ones are shown in a second colour).

YOU WILL LEARN
- Series: evenly spaced numbers
- Power: non-linear growth
- Bounds + Remap Numbers: mapping one range (lengths) onto another (angles)
- Pi multiplier: angles in radians

READ THE CANVAS LEFT TO RIGHT
Green = inputs you change, coloured boxes = numbered steps, blue = results.

SOURCE
Lucas Becker (runxel) - runxel/grasshopper-examples
gh/rotate_by_length.ghx @ 0e57586bdc
Licence: BlueOak-1.0.0 (see LICENCE panel)
Modified for the Almond parametric library: regrouped, relabelled and annotated; the geometric logic is unchanged.</item>
